== S1  CAUSALITY OF THE CONTROL — arm a split at the break minute ==
  A control minute BEFORE the break is selected using the knowledge that the day would
  later produce a booked break.  A control minute AFTER it is not: at the break bar the
  engine already knows the day qualified.  Only the AFTER half is a causal comparison.

| arm | split | n trades | break grossR | control grossR | paired Δ | day-clust t | note |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| a ALL minutes | TRAIN | 1622 | -0.0390 | +0.2173 | -0.2563 | -7.50 | as scored (look-ahead in membership) |
| a ALL minutes | VAL | 706 | +0.0827 | +0.2370 | -0.1543 | -3.59 | as scored (look-ahead in membership) |
| a BEFORE the break | TRAIN | 1168 | -0.0705 | +0.9830 | -1.0535 | -26.83 | NOT causal — membership uses the future |
| a BEFORE the break | VAL | 430 | +0.0778 | +1.0611 | -0.9833 | -22.63 | NOT causal — membership uses the future |
| a AFTER the break | TRAIN | 1621 | -0.0385 | +0.0249 | -0.0634 | -1.88 | **CAUSAL** — day membership already established |
| a AFTER the break | VAL | 705 | +0.0846 | +0.0590 | +0.0255 | +0.60 | **CAUSAL** — day membership already established |
| a AFTER, within 30 min | TRAIN | 1621 | -0.0385 | +0.0077 | -0.0462 | -1.89 | causal + clock-matched |
| a AFTER, within 30 min | VAL | 705 | +0.0846 | +0.1622 | -0.0776 | -2.24 | causal + clock-matched |

== S2  arm c is NOT a placebo ==
  The mark "entry_m - 15" exists only because a break happened at entry_m.  Its +1.2 R is
  the value of buying 15 minutes before a run you already know is coming — an ORACLE, and
  it is reported as one.  Coverage is also below the PREREG 80 % rail, so it is a
  DIAGNOSTIC and not a cell:
    TRAIN: 945/1622 = 58.3 % coverage, mean gross R +1.1964, target-hit 65.6 %
    VAL: 332/706 = 47.0 % coverage, mean gross R +1.2432, target-hit 64.5 %

